configure: the EXA version check preprocesses exa.h without xorg-server.h
first.  Since xorg-server 1.13, servermd.h refuses that with
"#error Drivers must include xorg-server.h before any other xserver
headers", the check fails, and the driver is built without EXA.  On a
server without XAA (1.19 has none, see 02.disable-xaa.patch) that leaves no
2D acceleration at all, although the log says "Acceleration enabled".

Upstream fixed the same check by including xorg-server.h first in later
releases of xf86-video-ati; this is the same change for 6.14.6.

--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -184,6 +184,7 @@
 if test "x$have_exa_h" = xyes; then
         AC_MSG_CHECKING([whether EXA version is at least 2.0.0])
         AC_PREPROC_IFELSE([AC_LANG_PROGRAM([[
+#include "xorg-server.h"
 #include "exa.h"
 #if EXA_VERSION_MAJOR < 2
 #error OLD EXA!
